<title>USA: Cone Blanchard seeks loans to reopen Vermont plant.</title>
<headline>Cone Blanchard seeks loans to reopen Vermont plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at the Cone Blanchard machine tool company in Windsor are headed to the unemployment office after the financially troubled company closed its doors Friday.</p>
<p>Cone Blanchard has been struggling for years and recently asked for loans from its employees. Company officers will meet state officials this week to try to find new financing to re-open the plant.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, 160 employees have been told to apply for unemployment benefits.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
